# GoTrading Core Conventions

## Code Generation Constraints

### No Bloat
- DO NOT generate extra classes, files, or utilities unless explicitly required
- Always evaluate if existing code can be reused before creating new
- Proactively suggest simplifications and removal of unused dependencies

### No Mock Data
- NEVER generate mock data or interval simulators
- Always wire frontend directly to real FastAPI endpoints at `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`
- If backend endpoint doesn't exist, create it — don't fake it

### Performance First (HFT Requirements)
- All Python backend code must be optimized for speed
- Use async loops, O(1) lookups, avoid blocking operations
- Use `msgpack` binary format over WebSockets instead of JSON

## Project Structure

```
gotrading/
├── .cursor/agents/       # Subagent definitions
├── algo-desk-central/    # READ-ONLY reference UI (Lovable)
└── gotrading/
    ├── backend/          # FastAPI + trading engine
    ├── frontend/         # Production Next.js app (EDIT THIS)
    ├── frontend_new/     # DEPRECATED - do not use
    ├── docs/             # Product documentation
    └── memory-bank/      # AI agent context files
```

## Progress Tracking

At the end of EVERY response, explicitly list:
1. **Completed:** Features/tasks just finished
2. **Pending:** Next items in queue

## Key Environment Variables

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `DATABASE_URL` | DB connection (default: sqlite:///./trading.db) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` | Backend URL for frontend |
| `PAPER_TRADING` | True for paper trading mode |
| `JWT_SECRET_KEY` | Auth token signing |
